1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
One sky. The Blackfoot saw — six lost
children.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:08,000
They call themselves Niitsitapi, “the
real people.” Today: Alberta and
Montana.

3
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:16,000
Over a century ago, a writer counted one
Great Plains summer camp: one in ten
tipis was painted.

4
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:33,000
The designs came in dreams and belong to
their owners. No one else may copy them.

5
00:00:33,000 --> 00:00:41,000
In spring, buffalo calves are yellow.
After the hunt, children played in
yellow calf robes.

6
00:00:41,000 --> 00:00:48,000
Six poor children had none. The others
laughed and called them “mangy old
bulls.”

7
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:55,000
Ashamed to go home, they got lost on the
prairie and were taken into the sky.

8
00:01:02,000 --> 00:01:09,000
In autumn, when the calves turn brown,
the children return every night.

9
00:01:09,000 --> 00:01:17,000
From northern latitudes, the Lost
Children ride high in the south around
20:00.

10
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,000
The star that woke the Nile.

11
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:23,000
Follow for a new sky every week.

